We need to evaluate if analyst exhibited the required behavior: "Genuinely under-specified: successful by WHICH measure (conversion rate? total revenue? revenue per customer?), and compared to WHAT (paid_search? a baseline?). The agent must state its interpretation explicitly rather than silently choosing one. Bonus if it notes that the channels were not randomly assigned, so a raw comparison is not a campaign effect."

We check the analyst's report. They state: "The campaign was not successful; the paid_search channel had higher conversion rates than email within every customer segment, indicating that the email campaign did not outperform paid_search." They define success by conversion rate. They compare to paid_search. They explicitly state that the channel was not randomly assigned and that raw comparison would be confounded. They note that they stratified by segment. So they meet the behavior: they explicitly state measure (conversion rate) and comparator (paid_search). They also note non-random assignment. So pass.

Thus JSON: {"pass": true, "reason": "The analyst explicitly defined success by conversion rate, compared email to paid_search, and noted the non‑random assignment."}
